// expect: refuse E_DuplicateFnName
// ONE RUN, ONE NAMESPACE: every name of a run is in scope in every body of
// the run, so two members of one name leave each reference meaning both. The
// module refuses its second `fn f`; a run refuses it the same way. Measured
// 2026-10-03 on boot 91257716: the second `f` shadowed the first and the
// program answered 2.
fn main() = {
  fn f() = 1
  fn f() = 2
  f()
}
